1
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:26,252
- So how's your mom, Ton?
- Same.

2
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:32,370
But my ex-goomar's cousin, I got her
to take care of her. Russian girl.

3
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:37,051
Who was telling me the Bevilaqua
kid has money from construction?

4
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:41,612
- Fucking Matthew was never any good.
- He sure cried like a baby.

5
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:45,130
I think the family was relieved
he got taken out.

6
00:02:45,340 --> 00:02:46,978
What are you gonna eat?

7
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:49,136
Hey, waiter!

8
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:55,893
That's the closest CW16 got Tony
to discussing the Bevilaqua murder?

9
00:02:56,109 --> 00:03:00,660
I think at this point it's time
to consider 16, Bonpensiero, compost.

10
00:03:01,509 --> 00:03:06,424
Bonpensiero was crucial
to the Webistics stock fraud case.

11
00:03:06,629 --> 00:03:08,665
So RICO-wise...

12
00:03:09,669 --> 00:03:12,741
...the airline tickets,
mail and wire fraud...

13
00:03:12,949 --> 00:03:15,543
...if the mother testifies
for immunity.

14
00:03:15,749 --> 00:03:18,104
Whose own mother's gonna testify?

15
00:03:18,629 --> 00:03:21,666
I say focus on his garbage business.

16
00:03:21,869 --> 00:03:26,545
- Extortion. Interstate trucking.
- It'll yield a prosecutable murder.

17
00:03:26,949 --> 00:03:31,181
Richie Aprile, no doubt about it,
the cartel had him whacked.

18
00:03:31,429 --> 00:03:35,183
But Tony shows diligence
when it comes to debugging.

19
00:03:35,869 --> 00:03:40,385
- What about the home?
- They talked in the basement.

20
00:03:40,589 --> 00:03:44,104
His own basement?
Where's the due diligence there?

21
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:46,305
Tony avoids business at home.

22
00:03:46,549 --> 00:03:51,669
He'll take somebody out by the pool.
Except there he fears parabolics.

23
00:03:51,869 --> 00:03:57,865
The basement has noisy AC ducts.
He turns on the air and he feels safe.

24
00:03:59,909 --> 00:04:04,107
"Surreptitiously enter and leave."
A "sneak and peek" warrant.

25
00:04:04,349 --> 00:04:07,466
- Correct.
- I said you could enter the basement.

26
00:04:07,669 --> 00:04:10,342
Do we have to impact
this family's privacy?

27
00:04:10,589 --> 00:04:14,662
First we determine
where to best place the wire.

28
00:04:14,909 --> 00:04:19,778
Then the listening device
will be fabricated and we install it.

29
00:04:20,029 --> 00:04:23,544
See that they limit both
entrances to the basement.

30
00:04:23,749 --> 00:04:26,980
It's not a Better Homes
and Gardens tour.

31
00:04:28,349 --> 00:04:29,862
Happy hunting.

32
00:04:42,229 --> 00:04:46,666
You know, the coffeemaker's got
to be plugged in for it to work!

33
00:04:48,069 --> 00:04:50,299
Same time as yesterday.

34
00:04:55,549 --> 00:04:58,461
I'm just going to the
stationery store.

35
00:04:58,669 --> 00:05:02,742
I'll be right back.
You don't gotta follow me. All right?

36
00:05:05,549 --> 00:05:10,384
To drop a wire there's got to be
nobody home for at least two hours.

37
00:05:10,589 --> 00:05:13,228
The maid is gone
on Tuesday afternoons.

38
00:05:13,469 --> 00:05:16,859
- Why?
- Classes to get her U.S. citizenship.

39
00:05:17,069 --> 00:05:19,458
She's gone from 1 till about 2:45.

40
00:05:19,789 --> 00:05:23,304
Class, then she and
her husband have lunch.

41
00:05:23,549 --> 00:05:26,382
He's applying for citizenship too.

42
00:05:26,749 --> 00:05:28,865
What's his name again?

43
00:05:29,309 --> 00:05:34,064
- Stasiu Wosilius.
- I'll run that by Anti-Terrorism.

44
00:05:34,309 --> 00:05:36,869
Carmela's gone on Tuesday. Tennis.

45
00:05:37,069 --> 00:05:41,984
We need somebody on her and everybody
that's got a key to the house.

46
00:05:42,189 --> 00:05:43,941
Daughter's at Columbia.

47
00:05:44,149 --> 00:05:48,062
Why risk it? She's 45 minutes
away. Put somebody on her.

48
00:05:48,309 --> 00:05:53,064
Anyone breaks for home, we need
to warn the team to get the hell out.

49
00:06:27,749 --> 00:06:32,698
- Unit 1, Baby Bing headed your way.
- Copy, control.

50
00:06:56,229 --> 00:06:59,665
Unit 2, you got Bada Bing
headed your way.

51
00:07:00,669 --> 00:07:03,627
Excuse me. Unit 3,
Mrs. Bing also in motion.

52
00:07:27,669 --> 00:07:32,663
- Do you have contact of Princess Bing?
- Roger, control.

53
00:07:43,749 --> 00:07:46,388
Unit 4, here comes the maid.
Gray Jetta.

54
00:07:46,629 --> 00:07:50,542
S.E. Team, the location's secure.
You have 90 minutes.

55
00:08:06,909 --> 00:08:10,060
Control, we're headed
into the sausage factory.

56
00:08:59,229 --> 00:09:01,424
- Just in time.
- Set a plate.

57
00:09:01,629 --> 00:09:03,062
You got it.

58
00:09:03,309 --> 00:09:07,382
I had him darn it in the shoulder,
like she wanted.

59
00:09:07,589 --> 00:09:10,820
- It shouldn't have torn.
- Beautiful coat.

60
00:09:11,029 --> 00:09:14,704
- What the fuck? Lunch is ready.
- I wash my hands.

61
00:09:14,949 --> 00:09:17,588
- You washed your hands.
- I tied my shoe.

62
00:09:17,789 --> 00:09:21,099
- So what?
- I can't stand touching shoelaces.

63
00:09:21,309 --> 00:09:25,507
Ever tie your shoes and notice
the ends of your laces are wet?

64
00:09:25,709 --> 00:09:29,861
- From what? Why would they be wet?
- I got no fucking idea.

65
00:09:30,109 --> 00:09:33,704
- You stand at the urinals...
- Come on, will you?

66
00:09:33,949 --> 00:09:36,668
He's asking, I'm telling.
It's important.

67
00:09:36,869 --> 00:09:40,418
Even if the lace is dry
and you don't touch the shoe.

68
00:09:40,629 --> 00:09:43,985
- Bacteria and virus migrate.
- You see this on TV?

69
00:09:44,229 --> 00:09:49,462
I gotta watch TV to figure out the
world? A men's shithouse is a sewer.

70
00:09:49,669 --> 00:09:54,185
In ladies' johns, you could eat
maple ice cream from the toilets.

71
00:09:54,389 --> 00:09:57,586
There's exceptions. But a men's?

72
00:09:57,829 --> 00:10:02,380
Piss all over the fucking floor.
Urinals jammed with cigarettes.

73
00:10:02,629 --> 00:10:07,066
They can pour all the ice they want,
it does nothing to kill germs.

74
00:10:07,309 --> 00:10:12,588
- Even if you don't drag the laces.
- Shut the fuck up!

75
00:10:14,909 --> 00:10:19,664
Mission control, I'm disabling
the line to the phone company.

76
00:10:21,549 --> 00:10:25,224
Phone line to the alarm
is neutralized. Cut it.

77
00:10:25,429 --> 00:10:28,341
Hold your breath.
I'm clipping the siren.

78
00:10:30,029 --> 00:10:32,259
Pick it, Wilson.

79
00:10:34,949 --> 00:10:39,340
Control, we're working on entry.
Estimate three to four minutes.

80
00:10:54,549 --> 00:10:56,540
You're not hungry?

81
00:10:57,429 --> 00:11:00,865
- Have some braciole.
- No, thanks.

82
00:11:01,069 --> 00:11:03,663
I got no appetite.

83
00:11:05,149 --> 00:11:08,664
- Today would've been our birthday.
- "Our" birthday?

84
00:11:10,549 --> 00:11:12,460
Oh, yeah.

85
00:11:12,709 --> 00:11:14,188
Spoons.

86
00:11:15,469 --> 00:11:18,427
- Happy birthday. How old are you?
- 51.

87
00:11:18,629 --> 00:11:20,665
Who came first, you or Spoons?

88
00:11:20,909 --> 00:11:24,026
Philip was my kid brother
by 11 minutes.

89
00:11:24,229 --> 00:11:27,062
Hey, it was a fucking tragedy.

90
00:11:28,069 --> 00:11:29,787
What're you gonna do?

91
00:11:29,989 --> 00:11:35,063
- It's the life we chose. Right, Pat?
- But my brother was never a heavy guy.

92
00:11:35,309 --> 00:11:38,858
I mean he was a sweet, gentle man.

93
00:11:39,349 --> 00:11:42,785
- Your brother was your twin brother?
- Philly.

94
00:11:43,269 --> 00:11:49,219
Friends, like us, called him Spoons.
Somebody whacked the kid.

95
00:11:49,909 --> 00:11:51,342
Before you came over.

96
00:11:51,549 --> 00:11:54,859
You big-mouthed fuck! Fuck!

97
00:11:55,709 --> 00:12:01,306
- You identical twin? Or the other kind?
- Identical.

98
00:12:01,549 --> 00:12:04,268
Here, have something to eat.

99
00:12:04,829 --> 00:12:10,301
There's a twin bond. Unless you
experienced it, you can't understand.

100
00:12:10,509 --> 00:12:14,184
- Okay with onions?
- Maybe it sounds crazy to you.

101
00:12:14,749 --> 00:12:18,662
Hey, nothing sounds crazy anymore.
The older I get...

102
00:12:19,149 --> 00:12:21,379
It's over, right?

103
00:12:26,109 --> 00:12:30,705
Don't it happen that twins can
die within days of each other?

104
00:12:30,949 --> 00:12:35,898
- That would've been okay, believe me.
- Come on! God forbid!

105
00:12:37,669 --> 00:12:42,265
- I miss him so much.
- Well, that's natural.

106
00:12:42,549 --> 00:12:46,667
You're with us. Leave the morbid
shit back at Junior's crew...

107
00:12:47,029 --> 00:12:48,860
...and have a happy birthday.

108
00:12:49,909 --> 00:12:51,661
Happy birthday.

109
00:12:51,909 --> 00:12:57,029
You wanna commit suicide? Tie your
shoes and have a bite of braciole.

110
00:12:59,069 --> 00:13:02,266
Hey, stonato, it's a joke. Come on!

111
00:13:07,949 --> 00:13:09,177
Hello!

112
00:13:10,549 --> 00:13:15,065
- God, don't transfer me now.
- Adriana La Cerva.

113
00:13:17,749 --> 00:13:20,309
How green was my fucking valley.

114
00:13:21,789 --> 00:13:22,983
Hi, Ed.

115
00:13:23,869 --> 00:13:27,578
This is my friend.
Adriana La Cerva, Ed Restuccia.

116
00:13:27,829 --> 00:13:32,698
I'm delighted to teach a pal of Carm's.
My most disciplined student.

117
00:13:32,949 --> 00:13:35,622
Perfect muscle tone
doesn't hurt either.

118
00:13:36,229 --> 00:13:38,504
I have to apologize, Carm.

119
00:13:38,749 --> 00:13:43,698
I thought I called everybody.
I won't be teaching here anymore.

120
00:13:43,949 --> 00:13:46,258
- Everything's all right?
- Basically.

121
00:13:46,469 --> 00:13:50,781
Kitty got this dot-com job
in San Diego, so we're moving.

122
00:13:51,029 --> 00:13:54,465
- I didn't even know you were married.
- Yeah.

123
00:13:55,149 --> 00:13:57,868
But you're in luck.
Birgit is taking over.

124
00:13:58,069 --> 00:14:01,505
- How wonderful.
- I never even played once.

125
00:14:01,709 --> 00:14:03,142
That's why you're here.

126
00:14:03,349 --> 00:14:07,865
Carm, I was wondering about
letters of recommendation...

127
00:14:17,429 --> 00:14:21,980
Kitty's company sells antiques,
so if you wanted a piece...

128
00:14:22,509 --> 00:14:26,980
- No antiques. My house is traditional.
- I'm cutting into your lesson.

129
00:14:27,229 --> 00:14:30,141
- Carmela, bye. Nice meeting you.
- Take care.

130
00:14:42,869 --> 00:14:45,781
Baby Bing is leaving school property.
On it.

131
00:14:47,909 --> 00:14:49,467
- Taking orders.
- Snapple.

132
00:14:49,709 --> 00:14:52,667
- Me too.
- I only got 2 bucks.

133
00:14:53,949 --> 00:14:56,099
Mrs. Celeste almost saw my board.

134
00:14:56,349 --> 00:15:01,059
- What a retard rule: "No boards."
- They can't see how useful boards are.

135
00:15:01,309 --> 00:15:05,382
In the cafeteria, each person
could just roll past the food...

136
00:15:05,589 --> 00:15:08,308
...and make their decisions.
- Yeah.

137
00:15:08,469 --> 00:15:10,266
That food tastes like ass.

138
00:15:17,469 --> 00:15:18,788
Hit it!

139
00:15:29,509 --> 00:15:32,069
- I had enough for one.
- Give me a hit.

140
00:15:32,309 --> 00:15:34,379
Don't backwash.

141
00:15:35,189 --> 00:15:39,785
- I won't do anything for this school.
- Mom's all, "Get involved."

142
00:15:39,989 --> 00:15:42,742
- I am. With boarding.
- It's Egon.

143
00:15:42,949 --> 00:15:44,143
Hey, Kosma!

144
00:15:50,749 --> 00:15:52,660
- Where you been?
- Orthodontist.

145
00:15:53,869 --> 00:15:56,258
- What class you ditching?
- Assembly.

146
00:15:56,509 --> 00:15:58,500
- Excellent jersey.
- Yeah.

147
00:15:58,749 --> 00:16:01,582
- Wait. You went out for JV ball?
- Yeah.

148
00:16:01,829 --> 00:16:05,788
Mr. Quadriplegic, remind me
not to visit you in the hospital.

149
00:16:05,989 --> 00:16:09,061
- That is a cool shirt.
- Yeah.

150
00:16:10,109 --> 00:16:13,101
- What position?
- Douche bag.

151
00:16:28,149 --> 00:16:29,377
Okay, cut it!

152
00:16:48,949 --> 00:16:50,905
Y'all should have come.

153
00:16:52,109 --> 00:16:55,988
- Where'd you go?
- We started off at Smoke's, as usual.

154
00:16:56,229 --> 00:16:58,982
But we wound up
at this place, Ruby Foo's...

155
00:16:59,229 --> 00:17:03,142
...round Broadway and 65th,
or something.

156
00:17:03,669 --> 00:17:07,901
It was so fun.
God, did I get hammered!

157
00:17:08,749 --> 00:17:13,903
- Don't you have a quiz today?
- Frosh Week. What do they expect?

158
00:17:14,509 --> 00:17:20,379
- I'll study now.
- I have a bio lab. I haven't read it.

159
00:17:22,109 --> 00:17:26,182
- Still miss New Jersey?
- It's only, like, half an hour away.

160
00:17:26,389 --> 00:17:29,699
It's just this transition.
It's a lot of work.

161
00:17:29,909 --> 00:17:34,380
New York is an experience
that unalterably changes a person.

162
00:17:34,589 --> 00:17:39,583
- It is really great.
- And all this freedom of college.

163
00:17:48,629 --> 00:17:53,145
- When did you have your last cocktail?
- 11:30 this morning.

164
00:17:53,749 --> 00:17:56,263
Jesus, Caitlin.

165
00:18:13,389 --> 00:18:19,066
- What is the most important right?
- Right to vote.

166
00:18:21,109 --> 00:18:25,660
Special capers from Italy.
Soprano kids don't like them.

167
00:18:26,749 --> 00:18:30,264
- Who wrote "The Star-Spangled Banner"?
- Martin Luther King.

168
00:18:30,509 --> 00:18:34,343
- Stasiu, you know this.
- I want to eat.

169
00:18:35,789 --> 00:18:37,268
Francis Scott Key.

170
00:18:41,109 --> 00:18:44,897
What holiday was celebrated
by the American colonists?

171
00:18:45,149 --> 00:18:47,458
- Martin Luther King.
- Stasiu!

172
00:18:47,709 --> 00:18:52,908
That's answer to number 49.
"Who was civil rights leader?"

173
00:18:55,549 --> 00:18:58,859
- Which sandwich is for you?
- I don't care.

174
00:19:13,269 --> 00:19:16,898
- Ready.
- Start shooting over here.

175
00:19:18,069 --> 00:19:23,189
Back in Lodz, I was an engineer
with 20 employees...

176
00:19:23,549 --> 00:19:28,065
...and a grant from the state
to do autonomous research.

177
00:19:28,269 --> 00:19:30,305
It bores you?

178
00:19:34,709 --> 00:19:38,941
Don't take those out. Put them
with capers. I take them home.

179
00:19:51,229 --> 00:19:53,106
That's just for Anthony Jr.

180
00:19:53,549 --> 00:19:57,428
- They're expecting WWlll.
- More likely the Colombo wars.

181
00:19:58,869 --> 00:20:02,703
He's got the Black & Decker.
I got one of those.

182
00:20:08,909 --> 00:20:13,027
- 120-gallon water heater.
- My house, we shiver after showers.

183
00:20:13,749 --> 00:20:17,105
Wait a minute. Go back.

184
00:20:17,749 --> 00:20:19,865
Look at the brown water, there.

185
00:20:20,109 --> 00:20:22,065
- What, lke?
- You don't see it?

186
00:20:23,349 --> 00:20:26,500
Creep forward.
Give us some magnification.

187
00:20:27,389 --> 00:20:28,902
That baby's gonna blow.

188
00:20:29,149 --> 00:20:32,186
Tony got about six months
left on that lining.

189
00:20:32,909 --> 00:20:38,666
- A shame we can't warn him.
- During his trial we can inform him.

190
00:20:38,869 --> 00:20:43,067
Except that's at least a year
from now. By that time, boom!

191
00:20:44,229 --> 00:20:46,948
Okay, now you see that lamp there?

192
00:21:04,069 --> 00:21:09,063
- Is that the C-140 microphone?
- They took sound readings. That's new.

193
00:21:09,309 --> 00:21:14,941
They talk where the AC is loudest.
That's where we're placing it.

194
00:21:37,669 --> 00:21:40,263
When's this puppy going in?

195
00:21:40,669 --> 00:21:42,022
Tomorrow.

196
00:22:02,069 --> 00:22:08,065
Okay, fellas and gals, our big day.
As I speak I have Baby Bing, on time.

197
00:22:08,629 --> 00:22:10,381
Handing off to you, George.

198
00:22:17,549 --> 00:22:20,859
I'm on Baby Bing's carpool vehicle.

199
00:22:29,149 --> 00:22:34,587
Furio Giunta Cadillac returning.
Went past me about five minutes ago.

200
00:22:34,829 --> 00:22:38,105
Der Bingle's up early.
He's in the Cadoo.

201
00:22:38,349 --> 00:22:42,137
- Copied. I got the handoff.
- Roger that.

202
00:23:05,909 --> 00:23:09,060
- How's the stock doing?
- Up three at the close.

203
00:23:09,309 --> 00:23:12,267
- Another two so far today.
- Beautiful.

204
00:23:12,509 --> 00:23:16,024
Listen, Ton,
I think we may have a problem.

205
00:23:16,229 --> 00:23:20,063
Log off. That cookie shit
makes me nervous.

206
00:23:20,749 --> 00:23:24,298
We may have a problem
about our friend, the twin.

207
00:23:24,469 --> 00:23:25,663
Yeah, so?

208
00:23:25,829 --> 00:23:28,866
Joey Fleiss hangs out at The Nest,
in Bloomfield.

209
00:23:29,109 --> 00:23:30,701
- Chip's place.
- Yeah.

210
00:23:31,069 --> 00:23:35,665
Our friend is a fixture there.
Joey says he's been into the booze.

211
00:23:35,869 --> 00:23:39,782
He's all fucked up.
They had to pick him up off the floor.

212
00:23:39,989 --> 00:23:45,905
Chip went to him. "Pat, what the fuck?
Can I do anything?" Etcetera.

213
00:23:46,149 --> 00:23:51,860
Pat launches this diatribe about how
one can smile and still be a villain.

214
00:23:52,109 --> 00:23:56,785
And that he knows how his brother
died and who's responsible.

215
00:23:57,029 --> 00:24:00,305
- He mention me by name?
- No. Me neither.

216
00:24:02,669 --> 00:24:06,025
- Hearing this?
- How would he know we clipped Spoons?

217
00:24:06,229 --> 00:24:10,222
- Twin telepathy?
- Somebody's putting ideas in his head.

218
00:24:15,749 --> 00:24:21,460
- Don't let us interfere with your game.
- May be a cop trying to flip him.

219
00:24:21,669 --> 00:24:25,457
Getting him worked up with theories.

220
00:24:27,749 --> 00:24:30,309
- He was talking weird.
- What do we do?

221
00:24:30,509 --> 00:24:34,263
We brought him over from Junior
to keep an eye on him.

222
00:24:34,709 --> 00:24:37,428
So that's what we'll keep doing.

223
00:24:37,629 --> 00:24:41,065
Make no mistake,
part of this guy loves you.

224
00:24:41,309 --> 00:24:44,107
But it's gotta be hard
coming in to work...

225
00:24:44,309 --> 00:24:48,302
...Iooking in the eyes of the guy
who had your brother whacked.

226
00:24:48,549 --> 00:24:51,268
And even having to smile.

227
00:24:51,709 --> 00:24:54,064
We always have the option.

228
00:25:00,069 --> 00:25:02,663
Mrs. Bing in motion.

229
00:25:03,349 --> 00:25:06,341
We got the housekeeper
then it's all yours.

230
00:25:19,909 --> 00:25:24,460
Hit low to high, Carmela!
And think about your grip.

231
00:25:25,269 --> 00:25:26,702
Fuck!

232
00:25:26,909 --> 00:25:30,697
No, that's good. Nice extension.

233
00:25:30,909 --> 00:25:32,979
Racket back, Carmela!
Come on!

234
00:25:37,629 --> 00:25:39,460
- Fuck.
- No, that's good.

235
00:25:39,709 --> 00:25:42,940
- Shouldn't that housekeeper be out?
- Take a look.

236
00:25:45,669 --> 00:25:47,864
Okay, guys, collect.

237
00:25:48,069 --> 00:25:51,982
Ade, let me work with you here.
Carm, you collect.

238
00:26:05,909 --> 00:26:09,265
Maid's car is still here.

239
00:26:12,469 --> 00:26:18,738
Okay, let's just focus.
Be serious and follow through.

240
00:26:19,349 --> 00:26:21,579
- Right! Almost.
- Okay.

241
00:26:29,269 --> 00:26:32,659
- Did you hear something?
- I don't know.

242
00:26:37,029 --> 00:26:41,705
We think we heard something
from inside the sausage factory.

243
00:26:41,909 --> 00:26:43,547
Hold your position.

244
00:26:46,749 --> 00:26:48,467
- Stand up straight.
- Okay.

245
00:26:48,669 --> 00:26:49,897
Here you go.

246
00:26:50,149 --> 00:26:54,586
See? Low to high.
All right, I can't do this with you.

247
00:26:54,829 --> 00:26:56,865
- Okay.
- Sorry.

248
00:27:11,469 --> 00:27:13,858
She's leaving the court.

249
00:27:24,709 --> 00:27:27,860
Der Bingle's leaving the Bing too.

250
00:27:33,149 --> 00:27:35,060
Hey, watch it!

251
00:27:41,349 --> 00:27:46,662
This does not look good. Mrs. Bing
bearing north on Grand View Avenue.

252
00:27:49,549 --> 00:27:53,667
She's on Boxwood Road.
She's heading toward the factory.

253
00:27:58,349 --> 00:28:02,740
Abort. Repeat, abort!
S.E. Team, get the hell out of there.

254
00:28:02,949 --> 00:28:07,659
Abort, Andy. It's not a go.
Repeat, we are not a go.

255
00:28:24,149 --> 00:28:28,904
- Must be a crisis with a kid.
- I place Baby Bing in the school.

256
00:28:29,829 --> 00:28:33,105
- Unit 5, report.
- A big Roger from this end too.

257
00:28:33,349 --> 00:28:38,218
She went in her room.
She told a friend she was gonna sleep.

258
00:28:38,429 --> 00:28:41,899
- Think somebody made us?
- I don't know.

259
00:28:42,109 --> 00:28:45,624
But we're finished for today,
ladies and gentlemen.

260
00:28:52,749 --> 00:28:58,699
Ten years. Ten fucking years he said
this thing would last! Motherfuck!

261
00:28:58,949 --> 00:29:04,467
- You said that. What are you doing?
- I told you not to put this shit here!

262
00:29:08,909 --> 00:29:10,740
Fuck!

263
00:29:10,949 --> 00:29:14,862
- Fuck!
- Never mind that. Save the pictures.

264
00:29:24,749 --> 00:29:27,900
The prom. Look at this.
Fucking ruined.

265
00:29:28,149 --> 00:29:33,860
- Mr. Ruggerio, thank God.
- The fucking water heater blew.

266
00:29:34,109 --> 00:29:37,658
Your guarantee's
gotta be expired by now.

267
00:29:38,549 --> 00:29:40,028
Madonna.

268
00:29:41,549 --> 00:29:44,507
- Do we have any idea what went down?
- No.

269
00:29:44,749 --> 00:29:47,707
- Family emergency.
- Plumber went there.

270
00:29:47,909 --> 00:29:51,663
Look, we don't have any idea
what happened.

271
00:29:51,829 --> 00:29:53,820
So let's not speculate.

272
00:29:54,469 --> 00:29:57,222
We're shit out of luck till Tuesday.

273
00:29:57,469 --> 00:30:00,779
We'll send somebody there
to stake the house out.

274
00:30:01,029 --> 00:30:03,702
Maybe we got a long-term problem.

275
00:30:03,949 --> 00:30:06,383
Well, we're heading back to Quantico.

276
00:30:06,549 --> 00:30:09,859
We got a job in Denver
day after tomorrow.

277
00:30:10,149 --> 00:30:12,458
A mosque.

278
00:30:18,789 --> 00:30:24,307
Morning. We'd like to get onto
your property to trim some growth...

279
00:30:24,549 --> 00:30:28,428
...that's posing a safety hazard
with the power lines.

280
00:30:28,629 --> 00:30:31,621
Okay. Go around the side.

281
00:30:31,829 --> 00:30:36,619
Records show our repair department
had some crews here yesterday.

282
00:30:36,829 --> 00:30:41,345
- Were you affected by the shortfalls?
- Yesterday?

283
00:30:43,149 --> 00:30:45,458
No.

284
00:30:46,309 --> 00:30:52,305
The people next door had some trucks
go up there. But, no, we're fine.

285
00:30:52,669 --> 00:30:56,821
How about them? Do you know
if everything's okay over there?

286
00:30:57,189 --> 00:30:59,464
As far as I know.

287
00:31:00,109 --> 00:31:04,227
- Well, we'll go talk to them.
- Probably you should.

288
00:31:05,309 --> 00:31:07,777
- They're in the M...
- Pardon?

289
00:31:09,989 --> 00:31:13,618
Nothing. They're different.

290
00:31:13,989 --> 00:31:17,823
For this neighborhood,
they're different, that's all.

291
00:31:18,309 --> 00:31:22,063
- Well, we'll get busy in the back.
- Thanks.

292
00:31:29,309 --> 00:31:33,143
- Still nothing out of the ordinary.
- Is the kid home sick?

293
00:31:35,309 --> 00:31:38,460
I don't see him. I see an arm,
piece of robe...

294
00:31:38,709 --> 00:31:42,588
...it could be Tony.
He's eating Sugar Pops.

295
00:31:43,109 --> 00:31:47,660
Wait, somebody just walked past
the kitchen window. It's the maid.

296
00:31:49,429 --> 00:31:51,863
- They're good.
- Fresh this morning.

297
00:31:52,069 --> 00:31:56,665
- How are things on Bloomfield?
- The Cuban was at the casino.

298
00:31:57,069 --> 00:32:01,506
Big John's okay with a 60-40 split
because we own the building.

299
00:32:01,989 --> 00:32:03,707
- What the hell?
- What?

300
00:32:09,589 --> 00:32:12,467
The fuck? Is that Pat Parisi?

301
00:32:14,749 --> 00:32:16,819
Oh, shit!

302
00:32:21,189 --> 00:32:23,066
What should we do?

303
00:32:33,949 --> 00:32:35,268
He's drunk!

304
00:32:35,469 --> 00:32:38,779
- I told John, "Look..."
- Let's talk downstairs.

305
00:32:49,509 --> 00:32:51,704
Motherfucker.

306
00:32:53,229 --> 00:32:55,902
I don't understand this at all.

307
00:32:56,989 --> 00:32:59,628
Cocksucker.

308
00:33:15,789 --> 00:33:18,223
What's up, lke?

309
00:33:19,109 --> 00:33:23,022
What happened at the Soprano house
was, the heater blew.

310
00:33:23,669 --> 00:33:26,900
Our unit saw Ruggerio
haul the old one out.

311
00:33:27,189 --> 00:33:30,818
- Ruggerio. A plumber?
- Why?

312
00:33:31,589 --> 00:33:34,945
My sister was friends
with Mrs. Ruggerio.

313
00:33:35,469 --> 00:33:39,223
Yeah, that's Mr. Ruggerio's
neighborhood.

314
00:33:39,589 --> 00:33:43,059
We have to get it in
before our warrant goes stale.

315
00:33:43,309 --> 00:33:48,019
Boy, we've had every one of Tony's
phones bugged for four years.

316
00:33:48,229 --> 00:33:53,303
- The guy says less than Harpo Marx.
- Next Tuesday the wire drop's a go.

317
00:33:57,909 --> 00:34:01,026
Der Bingle has left the building.

318
00:34:04,509 --> 00:34:06,306
They fucking made me.

319
00:34:06,909 --> 00:34:11,539
- Wire drop is still a go.
- Confirming access to switching box.

320
00:34:11,789 --> 00:34:13,620
I'm going in.

321
00:34:18,669 --> 00:34:22,218
Unit 2, Mrs. Bing in motion.

322
00:34:23,029 --> 00:34:26,738
- Just the maid and it's yours, team.
- Copy that.

323
00:34:28,709 --> 00:34:30,825
Siren wire is cut.

324
00:34:32,789 --> 00:34:35,940
The teacher knows nothing.

325
00:34:36,189 --> 00:34:40,865
Why do you quarrel with him always?
English is his first language...

326
00:34:41,109 --> 00:34:46,661
He waste our time with those
trick questions. "Stop. Men at work."

327
00:34:46,909 --> 00:34:51,061
How do we know it doesn't mean,
"Stop all men who are working"?

328
00:34:51,309 --> 00:34:53,618
He shouldn't have taken a point.

329
00:34:53,869 --> 00:34:57,464
He thinks I'm a hack cabbie
from Pakistan.

330
00:34:57,709 --> 00:35:03,022
- Please, where are you going?
- I'm going back to work!

331
00:35:13,829 --> 00:35:15,660
- Excuse me?
- You scared me.

332
00:35:15,909 --> 00:35:19,618
Sorry. Is the West Essex
Language School around here?

333
00:35:19,869 --> 00:35:23,225
- There.
- Is it coed?

334
00:35:23,629 --> 00:35:26,860
- What?
- You wouldn't happen to be Polish?

335
00:35:27,469 --> 00:35:29,107
Yes.

336
00:35:29,669 --> 00:35:32,581
That's...
My grandmother is Polish.

337
00:35:42,469 --> 00:35:44,619
It's locked today.

338
00:35:49,029 --> 00:35:50,542
- Yes?
- My grandmother...

339
00:35:50,789 --> 00:35:54,259
Excuse me. How can I help you, sir?

340
00:35:54,509 --> 00:36:00,698
I was wondering if I could ask
you about the school. How is it?

341
00:36:00,909 --> 00:36:05,266
Sweet mother of Jesus!
Look at her today.

342
00:36:13,589 --> 00:36:15,341
Hi, Ade!

343
00:36:15,549 --> 00:36:17,824
Hi, guys. Be back in a second.

344
00:36:18,069 --> 00:36:21,618
Listen to this now. "Hi, Ade!"

345
00:36:22,549 --> 00:36:23,777
Hi!

346
00:36:24,709 --> 00:36:26,028
- Hi.
- Hey, you.

347
00:36:27,869 --> 00:36:30,667
- I love those.
- Yeah?

348
00:36:30,909 --> 00:36:32,547
Oh, my God.

349
00:36:32,789 --> 00:36:35,178
- Where'd you get them?
- Near my house.

350
00:36:47,469 --> 00:36:50,461
- This table's been moved.
- From the flood.

351
00:36:50,709 --> 00:36:54,224
It's not under the duct anymore.
Should we move it?

352
00:36:54,429 --> 00:36:59,822
- Two, three feet? Who's gonna notice?
- No, wait. Somebody might.

353
00:37:00,069 --> 00:37:05,621
But normal course of events, Tony
will assume Carmela moved it back.

354
00:37:05,829 --> 00:37:09,378
- lf anybody even notices.
- Make an executive decision.

355
00:37:09,629 --> 00:37:13,508
- Grab an end.
- Easy.

356
00:37:13,709 --> 00:37:17,145
When she heard I was deferring,
she's like, "That's sketchy."

357
00:37:17,389 --> 00:37:20,222
Are you serious?

358
00:37:20,469 --> 00:37:23,666
Eric Scatino hates Montclair.
He's doing acid.

359
00:37:23,909 --> 00:37:27,140
God, he was so straight-edge.
Hi, Caitlin.

360
00:37:27,709 --> 00:37:28,903
Hi.

361
00:37:29,109 --> 00:37:33,022
This is Hunter,
my friend I was telling you about.

362
00:37:39,109 --> 00:37:41,020
Wow.

363
00:37:41,789 --> 00:37:43,939
Do you like Citron Jell-O shots?

364
00:37:44,189 --> 00:37:47,261
- I haven't had any alcohol in a week.
- I know.

365
00:37:47,509 --> 00:37:53,505
I was gonna say we should go to
Panchito's, then I remembered. Bad idea.

366
00:37:54,549 --> 00:37:58,428
- I went to the health center.
- For that problem swallowing?

367
00:37:58,669 --> 00:38:00,978
They gave me BuSpar.

368
00:38:01,189 --> 00:38:03,942
That's for anxiety, right?

369
00:38:04,109 --> 00:38:05,940
I guess.

370
00:38:06,309 --> 00:38:09,221
There was this weight lifter
on the subway.

371
00:38:09,469 --> 00:38:15,419
He was eating chicken parts and
spitting bones back in the container.

372
00:38:16,069 --> 00:38:18,424
And the whole car reeked.

373
00:38:18,629 --> 00:38:23,464
This blind man sitting next to him,
you could tell he felt invaded.

374
00:38:23,709 --> 00:38:28,385
We all did.
Everybody just stared straight ahead.

375
00:38:29,189 --> 00:38:30,508
New York.

376
00:39:14,509 --> 00:39:16,147
Where is everybody?

377
00:39:21,029 --> 00:39:23,827
- What're you doing?
- Receipts from Sunday.

378
00:39:37,269 --> 00:39:39,737
- You got a problem?
- What, Ton?

379
00:39:40,069 --> 00:39:43,744
I said, "Do you got a problem?"

380
00:39:45,309 --> 00:39:50,622
- With what, Ton?
- I heard you got a problem being here.

381
00:39:51,069 --> 00:39:52,422
I like being here.

382
00:39:52,789 --> 00:39:55,064
- You're sure?
- Yeah.

383
00:39:55,429 --> 00:39:57,579
- You're sure?
- Yeah.

384
00:39:57,789 --> 00:40:01,020
Don't say you're sure
if you're not sure.

385
00:40:07,269 --> 00:40:13,026
You bought your daughter a nice house?
After you came over with us?

386
00:40:14,029 --> 00:40:17,658
- Yeah, that's nice.
- Wonderful thing.

387
00:40:22,629 --> 00:40:26,019
And your brother, buon 'anima.

388
00:40:27,029 --> 00:40:31,819
You've recovered from that shit?
You put your grief behind you?

389
00:40:39,029 --> 00:40:41,623
You put your grief behind you?

390
00:40:43,909 --> 00:40:46,218
Let me hear you say it.

391
00:40:49,789 --> 00:40:52,622
I put the grief behind me.

392
00:40:54,229 --> 00:40:57,221
I'm gonna go get a coffee and a bun.

393
00:41:02,629 --> 00:41:07,259
You got a younger son too?
You ought to bring him to the house.

394
00:41:07,509 --> 00:41:11,024
We can get something to eat,
they can go in the pool.

395
00:41:21,389 --> 00:41:26,417
We'll have to leave this junk on the
table. Don't know where to put it.

396
00:41:28,469 --> 00:41:30,061
Control, you hearing me?

397
00:41:30,309 --> 00:41:34,621
- Loud and clear. Leave the factory.
- Roger that.

398
00:41:39,469 --> 00:41:43,428
Wire's in, Bobby. I'm good to go.

399
00:41:44,509 --> 00:41:48,582
- Control, we're in motion.
- Touchdown.

400
00:41:48,789 --> 00:41:52,020
Dig, Soprano! Come on!
You wanna join the team?

401
00:41:52,269 --> 00:41:56,228
You think it's all for show
and not for go? Dig in.

402
00:41:56,429 --> 00:42:00,627
You're out of there, George.
Unit 3, we're in.

403
00:42:21,069 --> 00:42:24,425
- So I got a job for you.
- Right.

404
00:42:24,629 --> 00:42:27,939
- Might get a little messy.
- I understand.

405
00:42:28,189 --> 00:42:31,625
- Wet work.
- All right.

406
00:42:32,189 --> 00:42:37,422
- I'll make it worth your while.
- I'm not worried.

407
00:42:40,029 --> 00:42:43,624
- Look over here.
- Minimization, 40 seconds.

408
00:42:46,469 --> 00:42:52,385
- The old one flooded the whole place.
- I can smell the mildew, you know?

409
00:42:53,109 --> 00:42:56,818
You're an engineer.
I figured you could rig a system...

410
00:42:57,069 --> 00:43:00,618
...some PVC shit or something,
so if it happens again...

411
00:43:00,869 --> 00:43:04,544
...you get the overflow
and put it over to a sump pump.

412
00:43:04,789 --> 00:43:06,780
Chip out the concrete.

413
00:43:06,989 --> 00:43:09,503
- Four-0.
- They're not discussing OC.

414
00:43:14,909 --> 00:43:18,026
In two minutes
we're allowed to check back in.

415
00:43:22,509 --> 00:43:25,023
What do you think?

416
00:43:25,269 --> 00:43:27,146
Whatever.

417
00:43:27,349 --> 00:43:29,419
Well, how much?

418
00:43:29,989 --> 00:43:35,939
Time, materials...
I don't know how to concoct estimate.

419
00:43:36,149 --> 00:43:39,425
Well, fair enough.

420
00:43:39,669 --> 00:43:44,823
- Let me get measure. Get started.
- All right.

421
00:43:45,429 --> 00:43:48,421
- Hi, Stasiu.
- Hello.

422
00:43:50,989 --> 00:43:54,265
- You gonna use this?
- lf you want it, take it.

423
00:43:54,509 --> 00:43:57,467
- No, you go ahead.
- Go ahead. I'll use the bike.

424
00:43:57,669 --> 00:44:00,661
I have to sort Meadow's laundry
anyway.

425
00:44:00,909 --> 00:44:03,981
Lilliana's making her a leg
of lamb to take.

426
00:44:04,189 --> 00:44:08,705
In Lodz, I had grant from the state
to do an autonomous research.

427
00:44:08,909 --> 00:44:11,946
Why don't you use it?
I'll take the bike.

428
00:44:12,149 --> 00:44:15,221
Jesus, already. No, you go ahead.

429
00:44:19,749 --> 00:44:24,027
Stas said he could smell
the mildew down here. Right, Stas?

430
00:44:25,709 --> 00:44:28,667
We've gotta let the place dry out.

431
00:44:37,429 --> 00:44:40,102
Got some girl
to take care of my mother.

432
00:44:40,309 --> 00:44:42,948
- Yeah, where'd you find her?
- Agency.

433
00:44:58,789 --> 00:45:01,223
Good coffee this morning.

434
00:45:02,109 --> 00:45:06,421
Vienna Roast.
It's not as acidic as the Italian.

435
00:45:07,069 --> 00:45:08,343
Cleaned me out.

436
00:45:08,589 --> 00:45:13,617
What you need is more roughage
overall in your diet.

437
00:45:14,549 --> 00:45:18,144
I've had something stuck
in my teeth for two days.

438
00:45:18,349 --> 00:45:21,227
You gotta use the other floss.

439
00:46:54,549 --> 00:46:55,538
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

440
00:46:55,709 --> 00:46:56,698
[ENGLISH]

441
00:48:57,316 --> 00:48:59,830
You got the crescent wrench?

442
00:49:00,076 --> 00:49:01,509
Nobody puts it back...

443
00:49:36,116 --> 00:49:37,515
Oh, my God!

444
00:49:37,756 --> 00:49:39,474
Tony!

445
00:49:43,276 --> 00:49:45,744
Oh, my God,
Tony, are you all right?

446
00:49:46,676 --> 00:49:48,906
- Uncle Ben.
- What happened?

447
00:50:23,076 --> 00:50:25,226
What are you doing here?

448
00:50:25,436 --> 00:50:29,748
We had to drive back. Someone stole
the VCR from the common room.

449
00:50:31,276 --> 00:50:34,188
Public Enemy!
That's a great movie.

450
00:50:34,396 --> 00:50:36,432
For our class. Just finished.

451
00:50:36,676 --> 00:50:38,109
We're out of here.

452
00:50:38,356 --> 00:50:40,824
$40,000 a year to watch movies?
Who's "we"?

453
00:50:41,036 --> 00:50:43,869
Just a friend from class, okay?

454
00:50:48,636 --> 00:50:51,230
- Your mom likes lavender.
- I'll be ready.

455
00:50:51,476 --> 00:50:52,750
Mr. Soprano?

456
00:50:52,996 --> 00:50:55,749
- I'm Noah Tannenbaum.
- How you doing?

457
00:50:55,956 --> 00:50:59,426
Thanks for letting us screen.
The speakers are great.

458
00:50:59,636 --> 00:51:01,194
You a film buff?

459
00:51:01,756 --> 00:51:06,272
Some say Hawks made the genre with
Scarface, but Cagney was modernity.

460
00:51:06,476 --> 00:51:09,434
Muni was not,
so I give the nod to Wellman.

461
00:51:09,676 --> 00:51:13,874
I'm just gonna grab that CD,
then let's hit the road.

462
00:51:18,876 --> 00:51:21,231
The last year for this course.

463
00:51:21,436 --> 00:51:26,749
"Hypercapitalist Self-Advancement
in the Era of the Studio System."

464
00:51:26,996 --> 00:51:30,909
So you guys, you and Meadow,
are you...?

465
00:51:31,116 --> 00:51:33,027
A little early to say.

466
00:51:34,516 --> 00:51:37,235
- What's your background, Noel?
- Noah.

467
00:51:37,476 --> 00:51:39,546
I'm from Los Angeles. West L.A.

468
00:51:39,796 --> 00:51:40,831
No, I mean...

469
00:51:41,076 --> 00:51:44,432
My family's in the business.
Show business.

470
00:51:44,676 --> 00:51:49,033
- Those old Tarzan movies?
- My dad's an entertainment lawyer.

471
00:51:49,236 --> 00:51:51,830
What I mean is, like, we're Italian.

472
00:51:52,036 --> 00:51:54,948
My dad's Jewish,
my mom's African-American.

473
00:51:55,396 --> 00:51:57,227
Tannenbaum, right.

474
00:51:57,436 --> 00:52:00,428
But on your application,
you checked Jewish?

475
00:52:00,636 --> 00:52:05,073
- No. They can't ask about religion.
- Right, of course.

476
00:52:05,316 --> 00:52:07,705
- What'd you check?
- African-American.

477
00:52:07,916 --> 00:52:10,191
So we get it. You're a ditsoon.

478
00:52:10,636 --> 00:52:12,547
Excuse me?

479
00:52:13,156 --> 00:52:16,148
Charcoal briquette? A melanzane?

480
00:52:16,396 --> 00:52:18,705
- What's your problem?
- You know.

481
00:52:18,916 --> 00:52:22,670
She didn't do you any favors
bringing you here.

482
00:52:22,876 --> 00:52:25,515
I don't know what she was thinking.

483
00:52:26,036 --> 00:52:28,027
I got associates who are black.

484
00:52:28,236 --> 00:52:30,875
I don't want their sons
with my daughter.

485
00:52:31,076 --> 00:52:32,191
Fuck you.

486
00:52:32,396 --> 00:52:34,705
See, that's what I want to avoid.

487
00:52:34,956 --> 00:52:39,427
So when my girl comes down,
you say it was nice to meet me.

488
00:52:39,676 --> 00:52:43,351
Then you'll take her to school
and say goodbye.

489
00:52:43,756 --> 00:52:45,633
Let's see the Garden State.

490
00:52:45,876 --> 00:52:50,074
We're gonna drop by Hunter's.
I want her to meet Noah.

491
00:52:51,836 --> 00:52:53,394
Later, Dad.

492
00:53:29,596 --> 00:53:34,386
- I don't got time for these attacks.
- It's been good for months.

493
00:53:34,596 --> 00:53:36,507
- lf you didn't instigate...
- Me?

494
00:53:36,716 --> 00:53:39,992
- He's just a friend.
- You didn't see them.

495
00:53:40,196 --> 00:53:42,505
You want her with him, keep it up.

496
00:53:42,756 --> 00:53:45,828
Play the race card,
she'll run into his arms.

497
00:53:46,036 --> 00:53:48,345
- Not if I cut off those arms.
- Stop.

498
00:53:50,116 --> 00:53:53,074
Let me deal with it,
if anybody's going to.

499
00:53:54,036 --> 00:53:57,824
Make things worse with your shit,
I'm gonna be pissed.

500
00:53:59,836 --> 00:54:03,749
I should call Cusamano.
You might need stitches.

501
00:54:07,636 --> 00:54:11,993
If my sisters ever brought home
a butterhead, my old man...

502
00:54:18,956 --> 00:54:20,309
Hey, Ma.

503
00:54:20,916 --> 00:54:22,065
Look who calls.

504
00:54:22,316 --> 00:54:24,989
Actually, I'm standing
in front of you.

505
00:54:25,516 --> 00:54:26,744
Hey.

506
00:54:27,676 --> 00:54:29,029
So how's it going?

507
00:54:29,236 --> 00:54:32,228
What do you care?
Out of sight, out of mind.

508
00:54:33,436 --> 00:54:38,874
I brought you some books on tape,
since you can't concentrate to read.

509
00:54:39,076 --> 00:54:42,034
I wish the Lord would take me now.

510
00:54:42,236 --> 00:54:46,468
In the meantime, I brought
The Horse Whisperer and Omerta.

511
00:54:46,716 --> 00:54:48,149
Why, what's wrong?

512
00:54:48,356 --> 00:54:52,474
You gonna freak out every time
I do something nice?

513
00:54:53,556 --> 00:54:54,784
What's this?

514
00:54:55,436 --> 00:54:58,314
She's finishing baby journals
from long ago.

515
00:54:58,556 --> 00:55:00,308
My idea.

516
00:55:01,676 --> 00:55:03,871
Oh yeah, I remember these.

517
00:55:04,116 --> 00:55:07,665
Carmela gave you one
for each of the kids.

518
00:55:08,276 --> 00:55:12,110
You're supposed to fill these out.
Twenty years, nothing!

519
00:55:12,316 --> 00:55:16,434
Now look here,
I don't like that kind of talk.

520
00:55:16,676 --> 00:55:18,348
Stop it, it upsets me.

521
00:55:18,596 --> 00:55:22,225
Carmela's ma returned these
to the kids filled with memories.

522
00:55:22,436 --> 00:55:26,952
- You can't write stuff for my kids?
- That's nobody's business.

523
00:55:27,156 --> 00:55:30,626
- Too busy feeling sorry for yourself.
- She'll do it.

524
00:55:30,876 --> 00:55:34,915
It's good for her. She knows that.
Keep her mind active.

525
00:55:35,156 --> 00:55:38,865
Why do anything if there's
nothing in it for her?

526
00:55:39,396 --> 00:55:41,307
Listen up.

527
00:55:41,556 --> 00:55:44,116
Concentrate. I know it's difficult.

528
00:55:44,436 --> 00:55:47,473
- Remember the plane tickets?
- They were stolen.

529
00:55:47,836 --> 00:55:52,193
Did you say that, or did the feds?
What did you tell them?

530
00:55:52,396 --> 00:55:53,624
What did I do?

531
00:55:53,836 --> 00:55:57,351
They're trying to build
a RICO case against me.

532
00:55:57,596 --> 00:56:00,349
What will you say
on the witness stand?

533
00:56:00,556 --> 00:56:04,185
They only let you go
to get your cooperation.

534
00:56:04,916 --> 00:56:09,114
Don't wave your hanky at me.
What will you say from now on?

535
00:56:09,356 --> 00:56:12,234
I never stated those tickets
were stolen.

536
00:56:12,436 --> 00:56:14,825
Barb'll testify. You back her up.

537
00:56:15,036 --> 00:56:18,346
I should have kept my mouth shut,
like a mute.

538
00:56:18,596 --> 00:56:21,633
In the future, any deal they make...

539
00:56:21,876 --> 00:56:24,151
...you keep your mouth shut.

540
00:56:27,796 --> 00:56:32,790
For a year I didn't speak to you.
Maybe I should have kept it that way.

541
00:56:34,436 --> 00:56:36,666
Fuck it. Do what you want.

542
00:57:20,436 --> 00:57:22,506
Did you say something to Noah?

543
00:57:22,676 --> 00:57:24,553
If you're smart, keep walking.

544
00:57:24,916 --> 00:57:26,713
You did. What did you say?

545
00:57:26,956 --> 00:57:30,665
He was quiet at Hunter's.
Now he's sitting in the car.

546
00:57:30,876 --> 00:57:33,993
You didn't hear?
Maybe if I say it in Swahili!

547
00:57:34,436 --> 00:57:37,428
- Meadow, can you come up here?
- What?

548
00:57:37,636 --> 00:57:40,514
I need your help with this clasp.

549
00:57:42,996 --> 00:57:44,714
That ain 't our beer.

550
00:57:45,236 --> 00:57:47,431
It's good, and cheaper than yours.

551
00:57:47,876 --> 00:57:49,594
Is my laundry done?

552
00:57:50,476 --> 00:57:54,594
I can 't help it if I have to buy
from Schemer Burns.

553
00:57:54,756 --> 00:57:56,189
You're yellow!

554
00:57:57,596 --> 00:57:59,746
You ain 't gonna slug me, are you?

555
00:58:24,076 --> 00:58:25,748
What?

556
00:58:29,116 --> 00:58:31,107
Your mother died.

557
00:58:31,356 --> 00:58:33,108
You're kidding.

558
00:58:34,716 --> 00:58:36,513
I mean...

559
00:58:37,676 --> 00:58:41,225
- Jesus Christ.
- Svetlana just called.

560
00:58:41,476 --> 00:58:45,469
She said that after dinner
your mother went upstairs.

561
00:58:45,676 --> 00:58:49,669
When Svetlana came up,
your mother was under the covers.

562
00:58:50,516 --> 00:58:53,667
Svetlana thought she was asleep.

563
00:59:11,836 --> 00:59:14,714
- Svetlana's waiting for us.
- She's dead?

564
00:59:16,316 --> 00:59:18,546
I'm sorry, Dad.

565
00:59:20,676 --> 00:59:23,110
- That your mom died.
- Me too.

566
00:59:23,316 --> 00:59:25,511
Your grandmother loved you.

567
00:59:25,756 --> 00:59:29,829
She loved both you two. Very much.

568
01:00:07,596 --> 01:00:10,588
- They just remove.
- We saw.

569
01:00:10,996 --> 01:00:13,226
She was in no pain, Tony.

570
01:00:13,436 --> 01:00:16,587
- What about the cause of death?
- Massive stroke.

571
01:00:17,116 --> 01:00:19,072
Yeah.

572
01:00:19,276 --> 01:00:22,905
She will not be finishing journal.
I break promise.

573
01:00:23,116 --> 01:00:27,268
Is not often that these old
ones get away with something.

574
01:00:27,476 --> 01:00:29,432
A journal?

575
01:00:29,636 --> 01:00:31,035
Nothing.

576
01:00:32,916 --> 01:00:38,195
Those Granny Remembers books you
bought her when the kids were born.

577
01:00:38,716 --> 01:00:40,866
She never touched them.

578
01:00:45,036 --> 01:00:46,435
What's your beef?

579
01:00:46,636 --> 01:00:48,115
Asshole Robert Frost.

580
01:00:48,356 --> 01:00:53,225
How am I even supposed to know
what this means? Like I even care.

581
01:00:57,476 --> 01:01:00,036
"Stopping by Woods
on a Snowy Evening."

582
01:01:00,276 --> 01:01:02,836
I'm glad I'm not in
high school anymore.

583
01:01:03,036 --> 01:01:04,594
- You read this?
- Sure.

584
01:01:05,676 --> 01:01:08,429
What does it mean? It's due tomorrow.

585
01:01:08,636 --> 01:01:10,035
What does it mean?

586
01:01:10,236 --> 01:01:13,273
The woods are lovely, dark and deep
But I have promises to keep

587
01:01:13,516 --> 01:01:15,791
And miles to go before I sleep

588
01:01:15,996 --> 01:01:18,146
Okay, look. Where is he?

589
01:01:18,476 --> 01:01:22,310
- In a field, on a horse.
- Not on a horse. It has bells.

590
01:01:22,516 --> 01:01:24,825
- So?
- What kind of horse has bells?

591
01:01:25,076 --> 01:01:28,034
I don't know.
Give me the fucking answer.

592
01:01:28,276 --> 01:01:31,632
A horse that's pulling a sleigh.

593
01:01:32,676 --> 01:01:37,431
It's a Thanksgiving poem? Like "Over
the River and Through the Woods"?

594
01:01:37,636 --> 01:01:41,345
It's not Thanksgiving.
What's covering the field?

595
01:01:41,556 --> 01:01:44,992
- Snow?
- And what does snow symbolize?

596
01:01:45,276 --> 01:01:46,265
Christmas?

597
01:01:46,476 --> 01:01:47,829
Hello?

598
01:01:48,076 --> 01:01:50,749
Cold? Endless white?

599
01:01:50,996 --> 01:01:53,146
- Endless nothing?
- I don't know!

600
01:01:53,356 --> 01:01:55,312
- Death!
- I thought black was death.

601
01:01:55,516 --> 01:01:59,475
- Miles to go before he sleeps.
- He's far from his house.

602
01:01:59,676 --> 01:02:03,908
The sleep of death.
He's talking about his own death...

603
01:02:04,116 --> 01:02:07,153
...which has yet to come,
but will come.

604
01:02:07,436 --> 01:02:09,506
That's fucked up.

605
01:02:10,276 --> 01:02:11,994
Gotta go.

606
01:02:12,836 --> 01:02:16,306
- I thought black was death.
- White too.

607
01:02:16,796 --> 01:02:19,151
I'm coming, I'm coming.

608
01:02:44,116 --> 01:02:46,107
Grandma?

609
01:02:48,676 --> 01:02:51,713
- I can 't believe it.
- What're you gonna do?

610
01:02:52,876 --> 01:02:56,994
- I'll call Janice.
- Meet you at Cozzerelli's around noon.

611
01:02:57,876 --> 01:03:02,711
- I already called.
- Ma didn't want any kind of service.

612
01:03:03,116 --> 01:03:07,109
So we'll pick out a simple urn
or whatever.

613
01:03:07,316 --> 01:03:09,113
I'll see you there.

614
01:03:28,556 --> 01:03:30,990
Proshai, Livushka.

615
01:03:31,236 --> 01:03:33,067
Which means what?

616
01:03:33,316 --> 01:03:35,876
Goodbye, little Livia.

617
01:03:40,236 --> 01:03:44,229
He's been in this situation
a million times.

618
01:03:44,436 --> 01:03:48,509
We'll see what happens.
There he is, pulling that in.

619
01:03:48,756 --> 01:03:51,350
He's got the eye of the tiger.

620
01:03:51,676 --> 01:03:53,507
- Ton.
- Anthony, turn it off.

621
01:03:53,756 --> 01:03:55,633
I'm sorry.

622
01:03:57,276 --> 01:04:00,427
We all know how much you loved her.

623
01:04:04,036 --> 01:04:05,754
Thanks.

624
01:04:10,236 --> 01:04:14,070
- I can imagine how you feel.
- Yeah, well...

625
01:04:14,476 --> 01:04:16,512
What're you gonna do?

626
01:04:16,916 --> 01:04:18,872
I'm sorry, T.

627
01:04:34,716 --> 01:04:36,547
What're you gonna do?

628
01:04:39,876 --> 01:04:43,505
- At least she didn't suffer.
- That's right.

629
01:04:47,276 --> 01:04:49,392
My God!

630
01:04:50,196 --> 01:04:52,585
What next, huh?

631
01:04:54,956 --> 01:04:56,833
How's Tony taking it?

632
01:04:57,076 --> 01:04:59,909
What the fuck?!
Goddamn fucking bitch!

633
01:05:00,116 --> 01:05:06,430
She was awful. How do I tell my kids
their aunt won't come to a funeral?

634
01:05:06,636 --> 01:05:07,989
I'll handle it.

635
01:05:14,156 --> 01:05:17,751
Then he goes,
"You gotta work on Columbus Day."

636
01:05:17,996 --> 01:05:19,952
Eat your eggs, baby.

637
01:05:23,076 --> 01:05:24,225
Ace Garage.

638
01:05:24,476 --> 01:05:28,105
You're not coming to your mother's
fucking funeral?

639
01:05:28,356 --> 01:05:30,824
- May I speak?
- Our sister's sobbing!

640
01:05:31,076 --> 01:05:32,828
May I speak?

641
01:05:33,076 --> 01:05:35,351
Go the fuck ahead!

642
01:05:36,436 --> 01:05:39,872
You may recall that I have
good and valid reasons...

643
01:05:40,116 --> 01:05:42,630
...not to enter the state
of New Jersey.

644
01:05:42,836 --> 01:05:45,145
That case is colder than your tit.

645
01:05:45,356 --> 01:05:48,075
It'd be good to show up.
Nothing to hide.

646
01:05:48,316 --> 01:05:51,035
- I don't do well at funerals.
- Who does?

647
01:05:51,436 --> 01:05:54,712
- You don't wanna leave your chair.
- I'll hang up!

648
01:05:54,916 --> 01:05:59,194
She didn't want a funeral,
but can't you sit with your family?

649
01:05:59,396 --> 01:06:03,309
- She was your mother!
- For us working folk...

650
01:06:03,516 --> 01:06:05,188
Woody Guthrie over here.

651
01:06:05,796 --> 01:06:10,551
- They got special rates for deaths.
- Yeah, half of full fare...

652
01:06:10,796 --> 01:06:14,869
...which, at this late date,
comes to $ 1100.

653
01:06:15,076 --> 01:06:18,193
Fully researched.
Fuck it, I'll pay it.

654
01:06:18,556 --> 01:06:22,310
- Can I bring my fiancé?
- Fuck that! One seat, coach!

655
01:06:22,516 --> 01:06:26,589
And don't breeze in
when it's time to divide the estate!

656
01:06:26,796 --> 01:06:31,233
I know you think Ma 's got money
buried in the house!

657
01:06:33,076 --> 01:06:35,954
- What about that other thing?
- Richie?

658
01:06:36,156 --> 01:06:40,274
He went into witness protection.
It's the truth. Right?

659
01:06:40,516 --> 01:06:43,428
Cozzerelli's Funeral Home.
Noon, tomorrow.

660
01:06:43,636 --> 01:06:47,709
Does Harpo know his grandmother died?
Him, I'll pay for.

661
01:06:47,956 --> 01:06:50,026
Bring him down. He's your son.

662
01:06:50,276 --> 01:06:54,633
Hal is on the pavers, Tony.
He's a street person.

663
01:06:54,836 --> 01:06:58,511
- I didn't know.
- You're not the only one with problems.

664
01:06:58,716 --> 01:07:00,149
Be there tomorrow.

665
01:07:17,276 --> 01:07:19,631
- Got a drink in the house?
- I wish...

666
01:07:19,836 --> 01:07:23,192
There you go with
that wishing stuff again!

667
01:07:24,396 --> 01:07:29,072
I wish you was a wishing well.
I'd tie a bucket to you and sink you.

668
01:07:29,316 --> 01:07:32,308
Maybe you found someone
you like better.

669
01:07:36,196 --> 01:07:39,233
Oh, Tommy! Let me make you
a cup of tea.

670
01:07:39,436 --> 01:07:43,634
I came over to give you something.
Here, take this.

671
01:07:43,876 --> 01:07:45,832
If you need more, just say so.

672
01:07:46,036 --> 01:07:48,675
- I'm caring for Ma.
- On two bits a week?

673
01:07:48,876 --> 01:07:50,707
Ma don 't go to nightclubs.

674
01:07:50,916 --> 01:07:53,555
How do you know? I used to dance.

675
01:07:53,756 --> 01:07:56,065
- Money's nothing to me.
- I guess not.

676
01:07:56,316 --> 01:08:00,150
But with no heart and no brains,
it's all you've got.

677
01:08:01,516 --> 01:08:04,349
Tommy! Tommy!

678
01:08:22,836 --> 01:08:25,031
His mother died last night.

679
01:08:25,276 --> 01:08:26,994
No shit?

680
01:08:49,676 --> 01:08:52,144
Ton, I'm so sorry to hear.

681
01:08:53,436 --> 01:08:55,791
What're you gonna do?

682
01:08:59,156 --> 01:09:01,306
I know how you feel.

683
01:09:02,716 --> 01:09:05,071
We lost Mom last year.

684
01:09:05,316 --> 01:09:07,432
You remember.

685
01:09:19,876 --> 01:09:23,869
- Least she didn't suffer.
- Ralphie, I need to talk to you.

686
01:09:24,116 --> 01:09:26,835
Albert, you too.

687
01:09:27,076 --> 01:09:28,828
Vito, have a sfogliatella.

688
01:09:29,036 --> 01:09:31,869
Carmela, she's gone.

689
01:09:34,756 --> 01:09:36,155
Come on.

690
01:09:44,196 --> 01:09:47,984
- Who torched one of Albert's trucks?
- One of the trucks?

691
01:09:48,196 --> 01:09:49,231
Be quiet.

692
01:09:49,436 --> 01:09:51,347
He lit up two of my dumpsters.

693
01:09:52,756 --> 01:09:57,068
What's the matter with you?
We're in the newspapers every week.

694
01:09:57,916 --> 01:10:01,795
My crew is in line for
the Raritan Township contract.

695
01:10:01,996 --> 01:10:04,271
They keep whispering to Albert!

696
01:10:04,516 --> 01:10:09,510
- What did you say? Whose crew?
- You put anyone you want over the crew.

697
01:10:09,716 --> 01:10:14,267
- You're a captain when I say you are.
- I'll turn up my hearing aid.

698
01:10:14,476 --> 01:10:17,309
Getting cute with me?
With my mother dead?

699
01:10:17,516 --> 01:10:21,907
Raritan Township recycling manager,
Joe Zachary.

700
01:10:22,156 --> 01:10:26,434
I'm in line for the contract,
but he's talking to Albert.

701
01:10:26,676 --> 01:10:30,385
- He's threatening to go to the EPA.
- He said that?

702
01:10:34,396 --> 01:10:36,034
All right, fix it.

703
01:10:36,916 --> 01:10:40,147
No more fires.

704
01:10:56,316 --> 01:10:59,831
I'm ditching Spanish.
Meet me by the trophy case.

705
01:11:00,036 --> 01:11:02,869
How could we possibly get busted?

706
01:11:03,076 --> 01:11:06,512
The boys' room by the stage?
They never check it.

707
01:11:16,476 --> 01:11:22,028
Mr. Soprano, Janice, Barb.
Please accept my condolences.

708
01:11:23,476 --> 01:11:25,785
I'll use all my skills.

709
01:11:25,996 --> 01:11:28,635
Don't go crazy. I mean, you know?

710
01:11:28,836 --> 01:11:32,875
Then we're not envisioning
any visitation hours for Mom?

711
01:11:33,116 --> 01:11:37,985
- She didn't want any service.
- I find that hard to accept.

712
01:11:40,396 --> 01:11:44,230
Is she still down
at the hospital morgue?

713
01:11:44,436 --> 01:11:48,349
We brought Mom here this morning.
She's downstairs.

714
01:11:51,676 --> 01:11:57,467
- There's gonna be a priest, right?
- Yeah, sure. A priest, I guess.

715
01:11:58,396 --> 01:11:59,590
When would that be?

716
01:11:59,796 --> 01:12:03,027
You're not having a Mass?
I'm not selling here.

717
01:12:03,236 --> 01:12:05,796
She was Catholic but not religious.

718
01:12:07,716 --> 01:12:10,628
I thought we'd have a shindig
at the house.

719
01:12:10,876 --> 01:12:14,869
After. So the grandkids could,
you know...

720
01:12:15,076 --> 01:12:17,032
I don't know.

721
01:12:19,676 --> 01:12:23,430
I know what Mom's wishes were,
but not to have a wake?

722
01:12:23,636 --> 01:12:27,345
We look like unloving children,
and cheapskates.

723
01:12:27,556 --> 01:12:29,945
Who gives a shit? It's her wishes.

724
01:12:30,156 --> 01:12:31,794
I wish to honor her.

725
01:12:31,996 --> 01:12:35,784
There's a lot of things I could say
that I won't!

726
01:12:39,796 --> 01:12:42,993
You think we should do something now?

727
01:12:43,196 --> 01:12:45,551
She used to picture her funeral.

728
01:12:45,876 --> 01:12:48,868
You wanna do something,
let's just do it.

729
01:12:49,116 --> 01:12:52,313
Cozzerelli, arrange it all.
Send me the bill.

730
01:12:52,516 --> 01:12:55,428
Tony, this all won't fall on you.

731
01:12:55,636 --> 01:12:58,833
I'll paint the overleaf
for the program.

732
01:12:59,276 --> 01:13:02,234
Motifs from the
Mexican Day of the Dead.

733
01:13:02,436 --> 01:13:05,712
One thing that I'd like to suggest:

734
01:13:05,916 --> 01:13:11,149
Everyone gathers and can voice
a remembrance or a feeling about Mom.

735
01:13:11,396 --> 01:13:14,513
I don't want any California bullshit.

736
01:13:14,756 --> 01:13:16,906
People can drink, they can eat.

737
01:13:17,116 --> 01:13:19,755
If they wanna yak about Ma, they can.

738
01:13:34,156 --> 01:13:38,946
No "I'm sorry, my condolences."
Nothing.

739
01:13:40,836 --> 01:13:43,031
Actually, that's good.

740
01:13:43,876 --> 01:13:48,188
It's a relief, you not saying nothing,
to tell the truth.

741
01:13:49,116 --> 01:13:52,153
You know, everybody else,
all bullshit.

742
01:13:59,236 --> 01:14:03,024
All right, here's the thing.
I'm glad she's dead.

743
01:14:03,276 --> 01:14:07,747
Not just glad.
I wished she'd die. Wished.

744
01:14:08,916 --> 01:14:14,229
Had this court case coming up.
She might've testified against me.

745
01:14:14,476 --> 01:14:19,391
So when I heard she was dead,
relief flooded into my veins.

746
01:14:23,276 --> 01:14:27,269
How do you feel about your mother
testifying against you?

747
01:14:27,516 --> 01:14:30,314
Come on, will you listen to yourself?

748
01:14:33,436 --> 01:14:35,825
Is that right, wishing her dead?

749
01:14:36,476 --> 01:14:38,990
- Is that being a good son?
- Good son?

750
01:14:39,196 --> 01:14:43,474
- Yeah, a good son. I mean, bad sons...
- Bad sons what?

751
01:14:43,716 --> 01:14:45,752
They should fucking die.

752
01:14:45,996 --> 01:14:49,511
That's a fucking
disgusting thing to be.

753
01:14:49,756 --> 01:14:53,351
Your kid, at Bard.
He better be a good son, right?

754
01:15:04,516 --> 01:15:08,429
You're right. Why should
I be good to that old bat?

755
01:15:08,636 --> 01:15:11,787
That fucking selfish, miserable cunt?

756
01:15:13,076 --> 01:15:16,352
She ruined my father's life.
Oh, yeah.

757
01:15:16,556 --> 01:15:21,152
But he wasn't her son.
What did she do to you?

758
01:15:21,396 --> 01:15:24,706
That's a matter of public record.
We both know.

759
01:15:24,916 --> 01:15:28,704
- You can't say it.
- She didn't know what she was doing.

760
01:15:28,916 --> 01:15:32,431
- You're letting her off.
- My uncle denies it.

761
01:15:32,636 --> 01:15:34,991
- He loves you.
- I know that!

762
01:15:35,196 --> 01:15:39,235
Grown children often wish
for an aged parent to die.

763
01:15:39,436 --> 01:15:43,395
It's not necessary for the parent
to testify against them.

764
01:15:43,876 --> 01:15:46,549
It's a taboo thought, but common.

765
01:15:47,276 --> 01:15:53,272
Particularly if the parent has lost
all capacity for joy at being alive.

766
01:16:00,676 --> 01:16:04,032
So we're probably done here, right?

767
01:16:04,236 --> 01:16:05,954
She's dead.

768
01:16:11,956 --> 01:16:14,914
- What is it?
- Tony's mother's wake is tonight.

769
01:16:16,556 --> 01:16:18,865
Want me to wear a wire?

770
01:16:20,156 --> 01:16:23,432
Sure. Need batteries?
Let's go to Office Depot.

771
01:16:33,476 --> 01:16:35,068
Janice?

772
01:16:36,436 --> 01:16:38,996
I'm downstairs.

773
01:16:41,796 --> 01:16:43,627
- Hi.
- Hey.

774
01:16:43,876 --> 01:16:47,835
- Mom would want a closed casket.
- Definitely.

775
01:16:48,076 --> 01:16:52,433
They usually put a picture
on the casket. What do you think?

776
01:16:52,636 --> 01:16:54,786
- Look at that.
- She's smiling.

777
01:16:54,996 --> 01:16:58,147
She looks normal.

778
01:16:58,356 --> 01:17:01,712
- It was us kids who turned her.
- One of us.

779
01:17:02,836 --> 01:17:05,031
Get the fuck off!

780
01:17:05,276 --> 01:17:07,392
All right, all right!

781
01:17:14,996 --> 01:17:16,554
Maybe you're right.

782
01:17:16,796 --> 01:17:20,675
My shrink says all women
aren't cut out to be mothers.

783
01:17:20,916 --> 01:17:23,146
- Is that a slam at me?
- No.

784
01:17:25,036 --> 01:17:29,552
If my father was in the circus,
maybe I'd turn out like Harp...

785
01:17:29,796 --> 01:17:30,945
Hal.

786
01:17:31,196 --> 01:17:32,834
- This is weird.
- What?

787
01:17:33,076 --> 01:17:36,625
None of my childhood artwork
is here anymore.

788
01:17:36,836 --> 01:17:38,588
Nor Barb's.

789
01:17:39,676 --> 01:17:41,826
Get the fuck out of here.

790
01:17:43,476 --> 01:17:47,628
"Anthony Soprano, 7th grade,
Mr. Martino. " I had him.

791
01:17:47,876 --> 01:17:52,108
"Why Fear Strikes Out by Jim Piersall
is a good book."

792
01:17:52,476 --> 01:17:55,036
Take a look. She only saved yours.

793
01:17:55,276 --> 01:17:58,473
What? Here's Barbara's
Communion certificate.

794
01:17:58,676 --> 01:18:02,066
- Here's her baby shoe.
- Yeah. That's it.

795
01:18:02,876 --> 01:18:04,787
Nothing of mine.

796
01:18:11,436 --> 01:18:16,191
Everybody agreed I had
"extraordinary visualization skills."

797
01:18:17,396 --> 01:18:21,105
Those pencil drawings
that I did of Grandpa?

798
01:18:22,036 --> 01:18:23,788
Good.

799
01:18:34,476 --> 01:18:36,546
Tony. Sorry.

800
01:18:39,636 --> 01:18:41,911
Tony, I'm sorry.

801
01:18:42,676 --> 01:18:44,189
He's disrespectful.

802
01:18:44,796 --> 01:18:46,593
Thanks for coming.

803
01:18:47,836 --> 01:18:51,226
Fucking motherfucking
pain in the fucking ass!

804
01:18:51,476 --> 01:18:54,354
Could we not, huh?
With the tantrums?

805
01:18:54,596 --> 01:18:56,791
For this I miss the Jets game?

806
01:18:59,676 --> 01:19:04,830
Did they say when your making ceremony
might happen, with this delay?

807
01:19:05,036 --> 01:19:09,712
Stop asking fucking questions.
If I knew, I couldn't tell you.

808
01:19:12,236 --> 01:19:14,113
Hit me. Hit me.

809
01:19:17,956 --> 01:19:22,711
Every little bit helps.
Anything to get through these events.

810
01:19:55,116 --> 01:19:56,344
Hey.

811
01:20:00,876 --> 01:20:02,992
- What a fucking blow.
- You too?

812
01:20:03,196 --> 01:20:05,505
I'm serious.

813
01:20:05,756 --> 01:20:08,475
Breaking the terms
of your house arrest?

814
01:20:09,036 --> 01:20:10,833
I got a dispensation.

815
01:20:11,036 --> 01:20:14,392
She's my sister-in-law, for chrissake.

816
01:20:14,996 --> 01:20:17,635
My dad's very ill too.

817
01:20:20,916 --> 01:20:24,306
Thanks. Thanks for coming.

818
01:20:25,836 --> 01:20:28,714
Allow me to express my condolences.

819
01:20:28,956 --> 01:20:30,469
Thanks, assemblyman.

820
01:20:30,716 --> 01:20:36,712
I met your mom once or twice.
That was a proud Newarker.

821
01:20:37,956 --> 01:20:39,674
Oh, hey. Reverend.

822
01:20:39,916 --> 01:20:44,148
My sympathies, Tony.
We talked about this day, did we not?

823
01:20:46,076 --> 01:20:49,830
You know State Assemblyman
Zellman, right? 8th Ward?

824
01:20:50,076 --> 01:20:51,873
Do I know him? You bet.

825
01:20:52,076 --> 01:20:54,351
Yes, we go way back.
How are you?

826
01:20:54,596 --> 01:20:56,188
Reverend.

827
01:21:02,276 --> 01:21:05,029
Uncle Jun? You all right?

828
01:21:05,236 --> 01:21:08,433
They're dropping like fucking flies.

829
01:21:08,676 --> 01:21:12,464
- It's that charcoal-broiled meat.
- Nobody told us!

830
01:21:12,676 --> 01:21:15,713
I'm kidding, you fuck.
What's the matter?

831
01:21:16,556 --> 01:21:19,753
- You wanted to talk?
- I gotta talk to your wife.

832
01:21:19,956 --> 01:21:21,230
Jun, come on.

833
01:21:21,476 --> 01:21:24,786
This is a funeral.
Enough of her soigné attitude.

834
01:21:36,316 --> 01:21:39,114
- What do you want?
- To use this sad occasion...

835
01:21:39,356 --> 01:21:42,871
...to put bitterness and
sore-headed feelings aside.

836
01:21:43,116 --> 01:21:47,826
I'll behave how Tony wants.
I don't want to add to his stress.

837
01:21:48,036 --> 01:21:50,675
- There they are.
- Hi, Uncle Jun.

838
01:21:50,916 --> 01:21:53,635
How's that surfboard I gave you?

839
01:21:55,676 --> 01:21:57,507
Tony's waiting.

840
01:22:07,676 --> 01:22:11,555
Ralphie Cifaretto got word to me.

841
01:22:18,636 --> 01:22:21,434
- What does he want?
- A bump up to captain.

842
01:22:21,636 --> 01:22:26,585
The kid's been a top earner since
that rat bastard went in the program.

843
01:22:26,796 --> 01:22:29,105
He whipped his crew into shape.

844
01:22:29,316 --> 01:22:33,707
Three months ago, the rat bastard
was the second coming.

845
01:22:33,916 --> 01:22:35,747
I'm boss. You forget.

846
01:22:35,956 --> 01:22:37,105
I forget nothing.

847
01:22:37,356 --> 01:22:41,872
- Don't make me say things we'd regret.
- Go ahead, I'm fed up.

848
01:22:43,236 --> 01:22:44,635
Hey.

849
01:22:44,836 --> 01:22:47,669
I'm on the street.
That's the arrangement.

850
01:22:47,916 --> 01:22:49,827
Stay home, clip coupons.

851
01:22:50,036 --> 01:22:53,631
Things are good,
but the economy's so robust...

852
01:22:53,876 --> 01:22:58,427
...you get credit for everything.
Chinks and housewives bet football.

853
01:22:58,636 --> 01:23:00,786
You better be finished.

854
01:23:23,196 --> 01:23:25,585
- Joe Zachary?
- Yeah.

855
01:23:25,796 --> 01:23:28,947
Oh, boys. No fires.

856
01:23:29,156 --> 01:23:31,829
Tony doesn't want any fires.

857
01:24:05,076 --> 01:24:07,874
I ain 't so tough.

858
01:24:12,756 --> 01:24:15,429
- Well, what do you think?
- Can 't say.

859
01:24:15,636 --> 01:24:17,069
Hope for the best.

860
01:24:17,516 --> 01:24:22,829
Doctor, this is Tom's mother,
brother, and Miss Doyle.

861
01:24:36,436 --> 01:24:38,825
The Lord bless her and keep her.

862
01:24:39,036 --> 01:24:44,030
The Lord make his face to shine
upon her and be gracious to her.

863
01:24:44,236 --> 01:24:48,468
The Lord lift up his countenance
upon her and give her peace.

864
01:24:49,356 --> 01:24:51,233
Amen.

865
01:24:59,636 --> 01:25:03,231
- Did you talk to her?
- She's sure you said something.

866
01:25:03,436 --> 01:25:06,314
He won't discuss it. He clams up.

867
01:25:08,276 --> 01:25:10,585
- Beautiful sendoff, T.
- Thank you.

868
01:25:21,996 --> 01:25:25,432
I want to thank you
for all you've done for her.

869
01:25:25,636 --> 01:25:29,231
She was much work.
In end, she defeated me.

870
01:25:29,836 --> 01:25:33,351
We won't need your services anymore.

871
01:25:33,596 --> 01:25:37,145
I'll be moving in.
If you could get your stuff out...

872
01:25:37,396 --> 01:25:38,590
...that'd be good.

873
01:25:38,796 --> 01:25:43,233
I stay there only during week,
when my fiancé has his children.

874
01:25:43,436 --> 01:25:47,793
Tony says I can continue situation
till Bill and me find house.

875
01:25:47,996 --> 01:25:52,228
Tony should have consulted me.
I'll be living at 55 Benedek...

876
01:25:52,436 --> 01:25:55,633
...while we deal with the estate.

877
01:25:55,836 --> 01:26:00,352
Speaking of which, my mom had
an extensive record collection.

878
01:26:00,596 --> 01:26:04,430
Caruso, Robert Merrill,
a shitload of Broadway shows.

879
01:26:04,636 --> 01:26:07,230
Do you know where they are?

880
01:26:07,436 --> 01:26:09,950
- She gave to me those records.
- What?

881
01:26:10,196 --> 01:26:13,745
She know I like American show tunes.
I didn't ask.

882
01:26:13,956 --> 01:26:17,710
They're my mother's records.
I feel very close to them.

883
01:26:18,116 --> 01:26:22,826
I don't want make a trouble,
but I have to respect her wishes.

884
01:26:23,076 --> 01:26:27,354
This is just about you bogarting
those discs for your ass.

885
01:26:27,596 --> 01:26:29,348
They're worth a fortune.

886
01:26:29,556 --> 01:26:31,626
I will not answer such here.

887
01:26:31,836 --> 01:26:37,513
I want the entire discography
back at the house by this weekend.

888
01:26:42,716 --> 01:26:44,911
Mrs. S.

889
01:26:45,836 --> 01:26:47,827
How are you?

890
01:26:48,436 --> 01:26:51,633
Sit down. How's your mother?

891
01:26:51,836 --> 01:26:54,873
- You call her every day.
- Mom passed away.

892
01:26:55,076 --> 01:26:58,068
Really? When?

893
01:26:59,676 --> 01:27:04,830
- About six months ago.
- Please, give her my regards.

894
01:27:05,036 --> 01:27:08,585
Is she still on that crazy diet?

895
01:27:13,676 --> 01:27:17,032
I brought you something.

896
01:27:17,476 --> 01:27:22,152
From my restaurant.
I don't know if you remember, Vesuvio?

897
01:27:23,836 --> 01:27:25,667
Mrs. S?

898
01:27:26,556 --> 01:27:27,909
What's the matter?

899
01:27:28,156 --> 01:27:31,114
After what my son did to you?

900
01:27:31,356 --> 01:27:34,826
- How can I look you in the face?
- What now?

901
01:27:35,036 --> 01:27:37,869
You don't blame him for the fire?

902
01:27:38,076 --> 01:27:40,351
Artie, what are you doing?

903
01:27:40,596 --> 01:27:44,430
Come on, we have people arriving.
Let's go.

904
01:27:44,636 --> 01:27:48,311
- Thank you so much. Thank you.
- I'm so sorry.

905
01:27:52,396 --> 01:27:53,670
Look at her.

906
01:27:53,916 --> 01:27:56,555
She's becoming a robot, like us.

907
01:27:56,756 --> 01:27:59,873
- I'm so sorry.
- At least she didn't suffer.

908
01:28:00,076 --> 01:28:02,795
All her innocence is gone.

909
01:28:10,796 --> 01:28:14,425
Then the Rabbi has to extol
the virtues of the deceased.

910
01:28:14,676 --> 01:28:18,555
The Rabbi says,
"I did not know this man. I'm new.

911
01:28:18,796 --> 01:28:21,026
You knew him. Say something good."

912
01:28:21,276 --> 01:28:23,870
Silence.
Goes on for about a minute.

913
01:28:24,116 --> 01:28:25,834
Finally, from the back:

914
01:28:26,036 --> 01:28:28,675
"His brother was worse."

915
01:28:41,356 --> 01:28:46,146
I walk out with the provolone,
and he thinks I smell like that!

916
01:28:52,076 --> 01:28:56,831
This Survivor. I should find the
winner, pull out a gun and say:

917
01:28:57,076 --> 01:29:02,434
"You're not gonna survive unless you
give me 25% of that million dollars."

918
01:29:02,636 --> 01:29:05,434
Not bad. We could find out
where they live.

919
01:29:05,636 --> 01:29:08,548
"See how you survive this,
pezzo di merda."

920
01:29:09,636 --> 01:29:13,595
Everyone, please.
May I have your attention?

921
01:29:14,036 --> 01:29:18,348
We would like to ask you all
to join us in the great room.

922
01:29:18,596 --> 01:29:22,509
Form a circle,
sit anywhere, get comfortable...

923
01:29:22,716 --> 01:29:26,834
...so that we can all be together
and share a remembrance...

924
01:29:27,036 --> 01:29:29,630
...about the woman
who brought us here.

925
01:29:29,836 --> 01:29:32,191
- Goddamn it.
- Please, join us.

926
01:29:33,836 --> 01:29:37,033
Paulie Gualtieri? Join us, please?

927
01:29:40,236 --> 01:29:42,113
Thank you.

928
01:29:44,956 --> 01:29:47,345
What the fuck did I say?

929
01:29:48,916 --> 01:29:52,545
If you'd rather,
I can invite them to her place.

930
01:29:53,356 --> 01:29:56,428
- Janice, what are you doing?
- Very good.

931
01:29:56,636 --> 01:30:00,629
We can all take a break from eating
for five minutes.

932
01:30:01,356 --> 01:30:06,384
Most of you will probably remember
that this was her favorite song.

933
01:30:06,876 --> 01:30:09,185
It might help us get rolling.

934
01:31:07,756 --> 01:31:09,553
Herman Rabkin?

935
01:31:15,436 --> 01:31:18,826
You two went back.
Almost to the pyramids.

936
01:31:22,476 --> 01:31:26,230
I guess what struck me most was...

937
01:31:26,476 --> 01:31:28,831
...she didn't mince words.

938
01:31:36,116 --> 01:31:40,473
Between brain and mouth,
there was no interlocutor.

939
01:31:51,556 --> 01:31:53,512
Anthony Jr.

940
01:31:55,476 --> 01:31:58,036
- I don't know what to say.
- Come on.

941
01:31:58,236 --> 01:32:00,147
Lay off, Janice. Move on.

942
01:32:02,276 --> 01:32:04,744
She was my best friend.

943
01:32:11,396 --> 01:32:15,071
If anybody died
or was in the hospital...

944
01:32:15,476 --> 01:32:19,594
...I'd get a call from Li
letting me know.

945
01:32:27,716 --> 01:32:31,106
Thank you, Fanny. Thank you.

946
01:32:37,076 --> 01:32:41,194
Okay. What's good for the goose...

947
01:32:43,596 --> 01:32:48,511
Most of you remember that I have
an extraordinary visual sense.

948
01:32:49,996 --> 01:32:53,750
As a child, Mom didn't let me
rest on those laurels.

949
01:32:54,356 --> 01:32:57,507
She didn't flatter me.

950
01:32:59,796 --> 01:33:04,153
She believed that wildflowers
blossom best...

951
01:33:04,396 --> 01:33:08,912
...among the rocks, with little water.

952
01:33:09,156 --> 01:33:11,226
She was tough.

953
01:33:11,476 --> 01:33:14,946
But she was right.

954
01:33:17,116 --> 01:33:20,074
She's the reason I make videos today.

955
01:33:27,836 --> 01:33:29,349
Tony?

956
01:33:30,436 --> 01:33:33,633
Maybe you'd like
to tell them how Ma...

957
01:33:33,876 --> 01:33:39,792
...saved all your childhood schoolwork
and none of mine or Barbara's.

958
01:33:41,716 --> 01:33:45,550
You just did. Wrap it up, Janice.

959
01:33:53,556 --> 01:33:56,229
I hear she didn't suffer.

960
01:33:56,516 --> 01:33:59,553
For that, we can be grateful.

961
01:34:00,276 --> 01:34:01,994
Thank you.

962
01:34:04,996 --> 01:34:10,468
They say there's no two people
on Earth exactly the same.

963
01:34:11,636 --> 01:34:16,710
No two faces,
no two sets of fingerprints.

964
01:34:16,956 --> 01:34:19,026
But do they know for sure?

965
01:34:19,236 --> 01:34:25,232
Because they would have to get
everybody together in one huge space.

966
01:34:25,516 --> 01:34:29,589
Obviously, that's not possible,
even with computers.

967
01:34:30,356 --> 01:34:35,430
They'd have to get everyone who
ever lived, not just the ones now.

968
01:34:35,636 --> 01:34:38,514
So they got no proof.
They got nothing.

969
01:34:51,036 --> 01:34:52,105
Hey.

970
01:34:56,996 --> 01:34:59,464
- So, Ton, she's dead.
- What?

971
01:35:03,396 --> 01:35:06,354
I guess our little secret...

972
01:35:07,116 --> 01:35:09,346
...dies with her.

973
01:35:22,156 --> 01:35:24,351
Hey, pick that up!

974
01:35:24,956 --> 01:35:26,947
What am I doing out here?

975
01:35:27,356 --> 01:35:31,395
Everyone's telling stories of her.
I got a beaut!

976
01:35:31,596 --> 01:35:33,473
Artie.

977
01:35:36,116 --> 01:35:38,266
Don't talk about that!

978
01:35:38,716 --> 01:35:44,712
She may have passed, but who's to say
there's not another just like her?

979
01:35:45,156 --> 01:35:49,115
Maybe not with the same fears
and paranoia, but...

980
01:35:49,356 --> 01:35:50,755
...the same.

981
01:35:55,036 --> 01:35:57,550
What I'm saying is...

982
01:36:04,796 --> 01:36:07,356
Thank you, Chris. Thank you.

983
01:36:18,596 --> 01:36:22,145
- This is such a crock of shit.
- Carmela!

984
01:36:22,356 --> 01:36:26,588
On one hand, I want to protect
my children from the truth.

985
01:36:26,796 --> 01:36:31,426
On the other, I'm saying,
"What kind of example am I setting?"

986
01:36:31,676 --> 01:36:35,589
Evading and smiling,
passing out cheese puffs.

987
01:36:35,796 --> 01:36:39,027
Over a woman who was
terribly dysfunctional.

988
01:36:39,276 --> 01:36:42,109
Who spread no cheer at all.

989
01:36:42,316 --> 01:36:44,910
- Carmela, be quiet.
- This is my house!

990
01:36:45,116 --> 01:36:47,550
- I'm leaving.
- Let her talk!

991
01:36:47,756 --> 01:36:50,224
I'll speak if I want! Who are you?

992
01:36:50,476 --> 01:36:52,865
Minister of Propaganda?

993
01:36:53,236 --> 01:36:57,115
We suffered for years
under the yoke of that woman.

994
01:36:57,356 --> 01:37:00,075
She estranged us
from our own daughter.

995
01:37:00,276 --> 01:37:04,747
Ruined I don't know how many
goddamned Christmases.

996
01:37:04,956 --> 01:37:08,949
No, don't hand me that! Bullshit!

997
01:37:09,276 --> 01:37:12,154
You wanted it, you got it.

998
01:37:12,916 --> 01:37:14,747
Hear, hear.

999
01:37:17,156 --> 01:37:20,307
From beyond the grave even.

1000
01:37:21,436 --> 01:37:23,586
This woman didn't want a funeral.

1001
01:37:23,756 --> 01:37:27,795
You all, her children,
ignored her wishes.

1002
01:37:27,996 --> 01:37:31,193
Only after she's dead, by the way.

1003
01:37:33,436 --> 01:37:37,748
She didn't want a funeral.
She didn't want remembrance.

1004
01:37:37,956 --> 01:37:38,945
Why?

1005
01:37:40,276 --> 01:37:42,915
She didn't think anybody would come!

1006
01:37:46,676 --> 01:37:49,395
She wouldn't write down
her memories...

1007
01:37:49,596 --> 01:37:53,509
...because nobody loved her
enough to read them.

1008
01:37:55,076 --> 01:37:57,385
She knew there was a problem.

1009
01:38:11,476 --> 01:38:15,230
There's desserts...

1010
01:38:15,476 --> 01:38:18,866
...in the dining room,
if anybody wants some.

1011
01:38:19,956 --> 01:38:22,106
Yes.

1012
01:38:22,356 --> 01:38:25,632
And they're all from Vesuvio.

1013
01:38:25,836 --> 01:38:31,035
Our new pastry chef, Bobby Vasquez.
Thanks.

1014
01:38:38,236 --> 01:38:41,626
Tommy? Mike's here.

1015
01:38:41,876 --> 01:38:44,185
He's come to see you.

1016
01:38:45,156 --> 01:38:48,228
You must like Mike
a lot better than me.

1017
01:38:48,476 --> 01:38:51,707
No, Tommy boy. You're my baby.

1018
01:38:51,916 --> 01:38:54,555
You're going to get well and strong.

1019
01:38:54,756 --> 01:38:57,748
All of us. Together again.

1020
01:38:58,356 --> 01:39:01,792
I'm almost glad this happened.

1021
01:39:13,156 --> 01:39:16,148
Yeah? This is Mike.

1022
01:39:16,396 --> 01:39:17,749
When?

1023
01:39:17,996 --> 01:39:20,829
You are? Fine.

1024
01:39:21,036 --> 01:39:23,231
- They're bringing Tom home.
- When?

1025
01:39:23,476 --> 01:39:26,434
- Right now. He's on his way.
- Wonderful!

1026
01:39:26,636 --> 01:39:31,756
I'll get his room ready.
I knew my baby would come home.

1027
01:41:45,236 --> 01:41:46,225
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

1028
01:41:46,396 --> 01:41:47,385
[ENGLISH]

